            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Feature name is validated as a single path component (empty/blank, dot segments, separators, padded whitespace, control chars) in service.go capture() before any sink call; the unsafe-name golden confirms nothing is created for ../escaped, a/b, and similar inputs.",
              "In the hook's ambiguous-change path, feature folders listed by the sink are re-validated with CheckPathComponent in unpersisted() before Read, so a hostile directory name under odd/review-receipts cannot cause traversal. It results in a denial, which is fail-closed.",
              "Features() returns only real directories; symlinks are excluded because DirEntry.IsDir is false for them. Read failures other than not-persisted deny the hook, so the new allow path is fail-closed.",
              "The new allow path requires byte-for-byte equality of persisted receipts, and the hook never writes in the ambiguous branch. Capture never overwrites differing files. Written files get mode 0600 via the existing Write path.",
              "--change together with --feature is refused with exit 1, so neither flag is silently ignored. A trailing --feature with no value counts as not given, the same as the baseline --change behavior, which falls through to auto-detect. This is a minor edge and not a security impact.",
              "The only changes to existing output are the multiple-active-changes remedy message, which now names --feature as well. That is part of the requested feature, and the goldens and tests are updated consistently."
            ]
          }
        }
      },
