            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 24 paths. --feature is parsed with explicit presence tracking, so an empty value is refused by name (golden test covers empty, blank, traversal, separator, dot-segment and padded names) rather than silently ignored.",
              "--change together with --feature is refused before a service is built, in every flag order, and writes nothing (golden and binary-level tests).",
              "Feature capture reuses the same idempotent persist path, never replaces differing bytes, and does not consult the change catalog (service and golden tests).",
              "The hook's single-change and zero-change branches are unchanged and never list features; with several changes it lists features only when a receipt is persisted under no change, and denies if the listing fails or a listed feature name is unsafe (feature_test.go).",
              "The only change to existing output is the multiple-change denial text, which now names --feature too; every affected golden file and unit-test expectation was updated to match.",
              "The fsstore Features listing returns only real directories, returns nothing when the folder is absent, and returns an error that names the folder when it cannot be read. A destination of unknown kind is refused without touching the filesystem."
